# Toggle

Toggle is a two-state button for options that can be turned on and off. Its native `aria-pressed` state, keyboard behavior, and focus ring work without extra wiring. Use a concise `aria-label` whenever the visible content is only an icon.

<DocsExample title="Toggle" source={toggleExampleSource} htmlSource={toggleExampleHtmlSource}><ToggleExample /></DocsExample>

## Variants and sizes

Use `variant="outline"` when the control needs a persistent boundary. The `sm`, `default`, and `lg` sizes accept text or icons; `icon-sm`, `icon`, and `icon-lg` create square icon controls. Toggle labels always use the system's `text-sm` scale.

## Controlled state

Set `controlled` when the parent owns `pressed`. The toggle calls `onpressedchange` with the requested next value but waits for the parent to update `pressed`; it does not change its own state. Toggle Group uses this mode for its items.
